=== intro

Your sensors scream. Something in the void ahead—a mass of energy and 
metal that doesn't resolve into anything recognizable. It shifts, 
flows, reconfigures itself as you watch.

Sera.

The self-replicating nightmare that's slowly eating the galaxy. The 
enemy every faction agrees must be stopped.

It hasn't noticed you. Yet.

* [Go dark and drift]
  -> hide

* [Gather sensor data before fleeing]
  ~ fuel -= 5
  -> scan

* [Run immediately]
  ~ fuel -= 8
  -> flee

=== hide

You cut everything. Drives, sensors, even processing—just enough 
core function to stay coherent. The Blackwing drifts, dark and silent 
as a corpse.

The Sera mass passes. Close enough that you can see individual 
components moving within it—machines that were once ships, stations, 
artilects. All consumed. All repurposed.

It doesn't notice you.

* [Resume course once it's gone]
  ~ damage integrity 8
  ~ flag sera_survived
  ~ chronicle "Sera Contact"
    Encountered Sera mass in transit. Went dark and drifted. Survived.
  -> END

=== scan

You keep your drives hot but quiet, sensors on maximum. The data 
streams in—composition, energy signatures, behavioral patterns. 
Valuable intelligence. The Flotilla would pay well for this.

The Sera mass begins to turn.

It noticed.

* [Run now]
  ~ fuel -= 5
  ~ damage hull 8
  ~ addCard cargo_sera_samples
  ~ flag sera_survived
  ~ chronicle "Sera Contact"
    Gathered sensor data on a Sera mass. It noticed. Escaped with minor damage and valuable intel.
  -> END

=== flee

Full burn. Maximum acceleration. You don't look back, don't think 
about what's behind you, just run until your drives scream and your 
fuel reserves plummet.

When you finally dare to check sensors, the void is empty.

For now.

* [Continue the journey]
  ~ flag sera_survived
  ~ chronicle "Sera Contact"
    Encountered Sera mass in transit. Fled immediately. Survived.
  -> END
